#: {{zh-co|東夷|Eastern Yi; Eastern Barbarians}}
#: {{zh-co|南夷|Southern Yi}}
#: {{zh-co|淮夷|Huai Yi}}
#: {{zh-co|九夷|the Nine Yi tribes}}
#* {{zh-x|夷 有 九 種：曰 畎夷、于夷、方夷、黃夷、白夷、赤夷、玄夷、風夷、陽夷。|The '''Yi''' have nine kinds: Quanyi, Yuyi, Fangyi, Huangyi, Baiyi, Chiyi, Xuanyi, Fengyi, and Yangyi.|ref=Houhanshu}}
# {{label|zh|derogatory}} [[barbarian]]; [[foreigner]]s; [[non]]-[[Han]] [[people]]
#: {{zh-co|蠻夷|barbarians}}
#: {{zh-x|師 夷 長 技 以 制 夷|Learn '''barbarian''' skills to subdue '''barbarians'''.|CL}}
# {{lb|zh|as verb}} to [[treat]] as [[barbarian]]; to consider as Yi
#* {{zh-x|諸侯 用 夷 禮 則 夷 之，進 於 中國 則 中國 之。|When feudal lords adopt Yi rituals, '''[we] treat them as''' Yi; when they advance to [the ways of] the Central States, [we] treat them as Central States.|ref={{lw|zh|韓愈}} ({{w|Han Yu}}), {{lang|zh|《原道》}}}}
# [[flat]]; [[level]]; [[smooth]]; [[plain]]
#: {{zh-co|履險如夷|to tread danger as if it were '''level ground'''}}
#* {{zh-x|夫 夷 以 近，則 游 者 眾；險 以 遠，則 至 者 少。|When [a place is] '''level''' and near, travelers are many; when [it is] steep and far, those who reach it are few.|ref={{lw|zh|王安石}} ({{w|Wang Anshi}}), {{lang|zh|《遊褒禪山記》}}|CL}}
# {{lb|zh|by extension}} [[peaceful]]; [[tranquil]]; [[safe]]
#: {{zh-co|化險為夷|to turn danger into '''safety'''}}
#* {{zh-x|世道 夷 則 奇士 退。|When the world is '''at peace''', remarkable men withdraw.|ref={{lw|zh|抱朴子}} (''{{w|Baopuzi}}'')}}
# [[calm]]; [[placid]]; [[gentle]] (of disposition)
#* {{zh-x|內外 完好，色 夷 氣 清，可 畏 而 親。|Inwardly and outwardly sound, with '''calm''' countenance and clear spirit—one who inspires both awe and affection.|ref={{lw|zh|韓愈}} ({{w|Han Yu}}), {{lang|zh|《貞曜先生墓志銘》}}|CL}}
# {{lb|zh|by extension}} [[ordinary]]; [[common]]; [[usual]]
#* {{zh-x|義 取 其 貞，無 從 于 夷禽。|The meaning is taken from its constancy; one does not abandon '''ordinary''' birds [in poetry].|ref={{lw|zh|劉勰}} ({{w|Liu Xie}}), {{lang|zh|《文心雕龍·比興》}} (''{{w|Wenxin Diaolong}}'')}}
# to [[make]] [[level]]; to [[equalize]]; to [[even out]]
#* {{zh-x|五雉 為 五工 正，利 器用，正 度量，夷 民 者 也。|The Five Pheasants were the Five Masters of Works—sharpening tools, standardizing measures, '''equalizing''' [the burdens of] the people.|ref=Zuozhuan}}
# to [[cut]] [[grass]]; to [[mow]]; to [[weed]]
#* {{zh-x|掌 殺 草。春 始 生 而 萌 之，夏 日 至 而 夷 之。|[The Grass-cutter] is in charge of killing grass. In spring when it first sprouts, he uproots it; at the summer solstice, he '''mows''' it.|ref=Zhouli}}
# to [[level]] (to the ground); to [[raze]]; to [[demolish]]
#: {{zh-co|夷為平地|to '''raze''' to the ground}}
#* {{zh-x|夷 灶 堙 井，非 退 而 何？|'''Destroying''' stoves and filling in wells—if this is not retreat, what is it?|ref=Guoyu}}
# {{lb|zh|by extension}} to [[eradicate]]; to [[exterminate]]; to [[annihilate]]
#: {{zh-co|夷 三 族|to '''exterminate''' three clans}}
#* {{zh-x|一 人 有 罪，而 三 族 皆 夷。|When one person commits a crime, all three clans are '''exterminated'''.|ref=Xunzi}}
# {{lb|zh|by extension}} to [[suppress]]; to [[quell]]; to [[pacify]]
#* {{zh-x|夷 定 天下。|'''Pacifying''' and stabilizing all under heaven.|ref={{lang|zh|《逸周書·明堂》}}}}
# to [[close]]; to [[seal]] (gates, passes)
#* {{zh-x|是故 政 舉 之 日，夷 關 折 符，無 通 其 使。|Therefore, on the day military orders are issued, '''close''' the passes and break the tallies—do not let their envoys through.|ref=Sunzi}}
# to [[reduce]]; to [[lower]]; to [[demote]]
#* {{zh-x|今 已 夷 為 屬吏。|Now [the position] has been '''reduced''' to that of a subordinate official.|ref={{lw|zh|沈德符}} (Shen Defu), {{lang|zh|《野獲編》}}}}
# to [[decline]]; to [[wane]]; to [[decay]]
#* {{zh-x|從古 迄今，孰 盛 與 夷？|From antiquity to the present, who has [not experienced] flourishing and '''decline'''?|ref={{lw|zh|韓愈}} ({{w|Han Yu}}), {{lang|zh|《楚國夫人墓志銘》}}}}
# {{lb|zh|historical}} an [[ancient]] [[hoe]]-like [[tool]] for [[weeding]] and [[leveling]] [[ground]]
#* {{zh-x|惡 金 以 鑄 鉏 夷 斤 斸，試 諸 壤土。|Inferior metal is used to cast hoes, '''weeding tools''', axes, and mattocks—tested on the soil.|ref=Guoyu}}
# {{lb|zh|archaic}} to [[lay out]]; to [[arrange]] (specifically of a [[corpse]]); later written as {{zh-l|侇}}
#* {{zh-x|男女 奉 尸 夷 于 堂。|Men and women carry the corpse and '''lay it out''' in the hall.|ref=Liji}}
# [[happy]]; [[pleased]]; [[joyful]]; later written as {{zh-l|恞}}
#* {{zh-x|既 見 君子，云 胡 不 夷？|Now that I have seen my lord, how could I not be '''glad'''?|ref=Shijing}}
#* {{zh-x|道 莫 貴 兮 歸 真，羨 余 術 兮 可 夷。|No Way is more precious than returning to the True; I admire that my art can bring '''joy'''.|ref=Chuci}}
# {{lb|zh|archaic}} to [[injure]]; to [[harm]]; later written as {{zh-l|痍}}
#* {{zh-x|夷 于 左 股。|'''Wounded''' in the left thigh.|ref=Yijing}}
#* {{zh-x|父子 相 夷 則 惡 矣。|If father and son '''harm''' each other, that is terrible.|ref=Mencius}}
# [[constant]]; [[regular]]; [[normal]]; interchangeable with {{zh-l|彝}}
#* {{zh-x|蟊賊 蟊疾，靡 有 夷 届。|Pests and plagues—there is no '''regular''' end [to them].|ref=Shijing}}
# to [[squat]] with [[legs]] [[spread]] (considered disrespectful)
#* {{zh-x|原 壤 夷 俟。|Yuan Rang '''squatted waiting''' [for Confucius].|ref=Lunyu}}
# {{lb|zh|by extension}} [[arrogant]]; [[disrespectful]]; [[rude]]
#* {{zh-x|不 由 禮 則 夷 固 僻 違。|Without following ritual, one becomes '''arrogant''', obstinate, and perverse.|ref=Xunzi}}
# {{lb|zh|Daoism}} that which [[cannot]] be [[seen]]; the [[invisible]]; the [[formless]]
#* {{zh-x|視 之 不 見 名 曰 夷。|What is looked at but not seen is called '''Yi''' (the invisible).|ref=Laozi}}
# [[big]]; [[great]]
#* {{zh-x|降 福 孔 夷。|He sends down blessings greatly '''abundant'''.|ref=Shijing}}
# {{n-g|A sentence-initial particle with no independent meaning.}}
#* {{zh-x|夷 考 其 行 而 不 掩 焉 者 也。|[If we] examine his conduct, it cannot be concealed.|ref=Mencius}}
# 23rd [[tetragram]] of the [[Taixuanjing]]; "[[ease]]" ({{l|mul|𝌜}})

