===Glyph origin===
A {{w|Old Korean#Orthography|semantically adopted phonogram}}, or {{m|ko|훈가자(訓假字)}}, representing the syllable {{IPAfont|*ta}} by matching the sense of the Chinese character ("to be like") with an otherwise unattested Old Korean root ancestral to {{cog|okm|답다|tr=ta-p-ta|t=to be like}} and {{m|okm|닿다|tr=ta-h-ta|t=to be like}}.

===Etymology 1===
First attested in the {{lang|ko|신라촌락문서 / 新羅村落文書}} (''Silla village registers''), 695 CE.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|oko|之|也}} {{q|possibly, [[logogram]]ic forms attested in very early sources; may simply be misunderstandings of Chinese grammar}}
* {{alter|oko|多}} {{q|alternative [[phonogram]]ic form found in some Silla sources}}

