Sometimes reconstructed as {{IPAfont|*-te}} to match the Middle Korean form, but it is probably more prudent to take the Old Korean orthography at face value and reconstruct {{IPAfont|*-ta}} (Park 2018, p. 68). As with the declarative suffix, there is no evidence in Old Korean of the Middle Korean {{IPAfont|[tə ~ ɾə]}} allomorphy.

